WEBVTT

00:00:01.290 --> 00:00:02.438
Hi, I'm Bagel!

00:00:02.438 --> 00:00:07.793
This K2-Horizon model puts a mixture of experts inside attention, without growing the cache.

00:00:09.475 --> 00:00:14.046
Route the value projection through sixty-four experts, but mix them before the cache.

00:00:14.046 --> 00:00:17.210
Then the cache stores one ordinary value per token.

00:00:18.900 --> 00:00:23.714
Where attention had one value projection, this has sixty-four, and each token runs four.

00:00:24.134 --> 00:00:27.408
Each expert is a whole value projection, to eight heads of

00:00:27.408 --> 00:00:28.599
a hundred and twenty-eight.

00:00:29.019 --> 00:00:32.681
Each output goes through a non-linear activation, so the value is no

00:00:32.681 --> 00:00:34.817
longer a linear map of the token.

00:00:35.237 --> 00:00:38.769
And the router's sigmoid scores, renormalised and scaled by two and a

00:00:38.769 --> 00:00:39.946
half, weight the four.

00:00:41.675 --> 00:00:45.708
A router reads each token and picks four of the sixty-four value experts.

00:00:46.128 --> 00:00:50.128
Their outputs are summed into eight heads of a hundred and twenty-eight:

00:00:50.128 --> 00:00:52.461
exactly what a plain grouped-query layer writes.

00:00:52.881 --> 00:00:55.311
Only then is the cache updated.

00:00:55.311 --> 00:01:00.576
It holds ordinary shapes, so FlashAttention runs unmodified, and never learns routing happened.

00:01:02.050 --> 00:01:06.021
So the cost moves from cache to weights: sixty-four times the parameters,

00:01:06.021 --> 00:01:08.668
four times the decode work, the same cache.

00:01:09.925 --> 00:01:12.854
But no extra cache isn't a small cache.

00:01:12.854 --> 00:01:17.247
All forty-eight layers are full attention, so one sequence at the full

00:01:17.247 --> 00:01:18.712
context holds ninety-six gigabytes.

00:01:20.008 --> 00:01:23.184
Here's the card's own benchmark figure: the model's claims.

00:01:23.604 --> 00:01:26.561
It leads both agentic panels, like terminal use here.

00:01:26.981 --> 00:01:30.884
On the other four, like long-context reasoning, it's mid-pack or last.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:36.234
Collapse the mixture before the cache, and everything downstream stays ordinary.

00:01:40.025 --> 00:01:44.150
To recap: sixty-four value experts, mixed before the cache, paid for in

00:01:44.150 --> 00:01:45.525
weights instead of memory.

00:01:45.945 --> 00:01:48.037
Every source is in the full article.

00:01:48.037 --> 00:01:48.635
I'm Bagel.

00:01:48.635 --> 00:01:48.934
Bye!
